  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates which lottery has a higher probability of a favorable (non-zero) outcome and prefers that one. The information relevant to the reason—probabilities of non-zero outcomes (50% for A, 25% for B)—matches what the individual considered. Furthermore, the individual’s justification (preferring A due to higher chance of winning something, avoiding zero) aligns directly with the rule of the decision reason (favoring the lottery with higher probability of a favorable outcome). The verbal report reflects both the relevant information and the same comparative probabilistic logic as the reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this decision reason.",
